      "section": "External Works – Example",
      "title": "External Works – Example: Federal Environment Agency",
      "summary": "The external works at the Federal Environment Agency in Dessau create a landscape that mediates between the building and the city. The design combines functional planting and plot enclosure with naturalistic landscape elements. Excavated material shapes the site; paths and paved areas also provide fire-service access. Surfaces include mosaic stone, waterbound paving, travertine, concrete, asphalt, and grass-jointed paving. Drainage connects paved-area gullies to existing rainwater pipes, while canteen roof runoff flows to a pond. Site furniture and works of art contribute to the overall design.",
